From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Drop the register storage class

C++17 removed 'register', and clang rejects it outright.

Upstream: the register hunk of e2f8d50c53102c618d675c3310e09a0e0bdf49cd,
merged after 1.5; the rest of that commit does not apply to 1.5
---
diff --git a/src/binio.cpp b/src/binio.cpp
--- a/src/binio.cpp
+++ b/src/binio.cpp
@@ -490,7 +490,7 @@
 void binostream::float2ieee_single(Float num, Byte *bytes)
 {
   long		sign;
-  register long	bits;
+  long		bits;
 
   if (num < 0) {	/* Can't distinguish a negative zero */
     sign = 0x80000000;
